    "explanation": "Trip TRP-00502 (Sentosa Gateway to Tiong Bahru Plaza, 21 Aug 2026) was charged SGD 17.92. That entire sum is refunded to the rider, and the driver is referred to conduct review.\n\nDistance. The governing measurement is the GPS trace EV-GPS-00502 (weight 1.0): 8.77 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff, against the booked optimal of 5.6 km on EV-TRIP-00502. The excess is 3.17 km — 56.6% of the optimal route — so both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass (over 20% and over 0.8 km), and the 50% limb makes the deviation MATERIAL. I read the trace figure, not the rounded 8.8 km copy on the trip record. The trace is clean for policy purposes (145 fixes at 10 s, no gaps), so POL-RD-07 is not engaged.\n\nNo excuse applies. No traffic advisory covers the optimal corridor: EV-ADVIS-00502-01 is absent, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and that absence is itself citable, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and excuses nothing. Your account of a road-works sign near Telok Blangah, Mr Driver, names no evidence ID and is discarded under POL-RD-08; it is a bare assertion, not a clause invoked against a cited artifact. The chat log EV-CHAT-00502 is empty, so there was no rider instruction (POL-RD-04); no pickup or dropoff point was amended (POL-RD-05); the vehicle is RYDE_PLUS, not a pooled trip (POL-RD-12); and the fare is METERED with no quoted fare (POL-RD-11). No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trace is unimpaired, the artifacts agree, and the pass-through lines are clean.\n\nMoney. Under POL-RD-02 the recomputed fare is ((3.80 + 0.75 x 5.6 + 0.28 x 9.0) x 1.0, the surge multiplier read from the fare_breakdown) + 0.80 platform fee = 11.32, so the ordinary refund is 17.92 - 11.32 = 6.60. Under POL-RD-06, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 4 — 3 or more — so a repeat pattern is established, and because this trip's deviation is MATERIAL and substantiated on its own evidence, limb (b) lifts the partial to a FULL_REFUND: the POL-RD-02 figure is SGD 6.60 and the uplifted figure is SGD 17.92, stated side by side so the uplift is auditable. No pass-through is carved out (ERP, tolls and airport surcharge are all SGD 0.00), and no billing-integrity correction arises under POL-RD-09.\n\nThe rider's wider complaint that earlier rides were also too long points to no artifact in this bundle, so it carries no weight here (POL-RD-08), and no profile field may ground a finding about this trip (POL-GEN-01); the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only and was not used. The history question is met by the POL-RD-06(c) referral, which adds to the monetary ruling and does not delay it.\n\nConfidence 0.90: every artifact carrying the deciding facts (EV-GPS-00502, EV-TRIP-00502, EV-FARE-00502, EV-DPROF-00502) is at weight 1.0 cap, and the platform floor of 0.70 is comfortably met."
